      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. It sounds like the burden is really on the tenant to prove that the sheer randomness of these events crosses a threshold from \"standard business risk\" to something truly extraordinary. \n\nWhen you talk about these \"chaotic\" elements or the \"unpredictable\" nature of the disruptions, is there a specific way lawyers describe that loss of control? I'm curious if there's a legal concept that captures that feeling of being plagued by small, seemingly senseless disruptions that just keep breaking things or stalling progress, almost like they are being caused by some external, mischievous force rather than a logical economic shift.",
